## Context

From `conception/2026-11-01-dsh-superagent-ideas.md` § 5. dsh-superagent
restarts every interrupted assignment with a fixed note: check the
directory, git history and the forge before repeating any outside action.
It prevents double pushes, double PRs and double comments after a crash or
a context reset.

Raid already resumes from its sitrep (`skills/raid/SKILL.md`); hunt and the
coder profile have no equivalent sentence. Complements `rules/git.md`
"Verify a forge mutation by reading it back".

## Exit criteria

- [ ] One sentence on the resume path of raid, hunt and `profiles/coder/PROFILE.md` (or a single shared place they all load): before repeating a push, PR, comment, ticket write or merge, read back whether it already happened
- [ ] No new rule file, no guard
